# Use git, not gh

Use `git` for branches, status, diff, log, commit, fetch, and push. Do not use the `gh` GitHub CLI (`gh pr create`, `gh issue`, `gh api`, …).

```bash
# BAD
gh pr create --title "..." --body "..."

# GOOD
git push -u origin HEAD
# then open the PR through GitLens / the git host, not gh
```

- Commit only when asked, with a message that says why.
- Push with `git push -u origin HEAD` when asked to publish the branch.
- Create or update pull requests through GitLens or the git host UI/API, never `gh`.
